# Scope

Follow `project-spec.md`. Do not re-litigate the stack.

- Web: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Zod, Zustand.
- API: Node, Express, TypeScript, Prisma, Zod. JWT via `jsonwebtoken`. Passwords via `bcrypt`.
- Data: PostgreSQL on Neon through Prisma. Files: Cloudflare R2. Web on Vercel. API on Zeabur. Cron: cron-job.org.
- Do not replace the API with Supabase, Firebase, or another BaaS, and do not move it to Vercel serverless.
- Do not add a second always-on service.
- The API stays client-agnostic so a future non-browser client can call it.

## Do not break
- Every user-data route checks that the caller owns the resource.
- No public R2 URLs. The API streams voice and image bytes after the ownership check.
- Zod schemas live in `packages/shared` and are shared by both apps.
- Timestamps stay UTC. "Today" is computed at read time from `timezone` and `day_start_time`.

## Out of scope
Do not build: AI categorization, transcription, a native app, password reset, email verification, search, offline capture or reading, export, account deletion, sharing text or images into the PWA, copying preview images into R2, transcoding voice to MP3.

If time slips, cut in this order only, and stop at the first cut that fits: Share Target, image capture, link-preview fetching (still save the URL), daily progress indicator. Do not cut auth, text/link/voice capture, categories, tags, day boundary, revival, or reminders.

## Decisions
Record each major choice in `DECISIONS.md`: what was chosen, what was rejected, and why, in terms the user can explain later.
